{"content_hash": "10085493b28de903", "version_id": 454, "article_id": 46, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "Panama hit by powerful 7.7 earthquake, buildings damaged", "title_zh": "巴拿马遭遇7.7级强震，多处建筑受损", "has_translation": true, "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c620r39zdp9wo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1677233860259-ce1a8e0f8498?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MXx8cG93ZXJmdWwlMjBtYWduaXR1ZGUlMjBlYXJ0aHF1YWtlfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE1OTQ2NTJ8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Çağlar Oskay on Unsplash", "author": "Çağlar Oskay", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@oskaycaglar?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-car-is-parked-in-front-of-a-destroyed-building-mmLtohu4qmE?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(73, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(111, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "69c1918b4164"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-09", "word_count": 276, "reading_minutes": 1.4, "lead": "A magnitude 7.7 earthquake struck Panama on Friday, damaging buildings and shaking a wide area. About 4.6 million people felt the tremors, and no deaths have been reported so far.", "lead_zh": "周五，巴拿马发生7.7级地震，导致建筑物受损，大片地区有震感。约460万人感受到震动，目前尚无人员死亡报告。", "preview": "The earthquake hit just before 15:00 local time on Friday, with its epicentre about 10km from the town of Pitaloza Arriba in south-central P", "preview_zh": "地震发生在当地时间周五15:00前不久，震中位于巴拿马中南部城镇皮塔洛萨阿里巴附近约10公里处。据美国地质调查局称，约460万人感受到中度至强烈震动，影响可能很广泛。此次地震深度仅12公里，这使得其地表影响更为严重。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 444, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/46/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 106.75, "size_bytes": 644256, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 321, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/454.json", "paragraphs": ["The earthquake hit just before 15:00 local time on Friday, with its epicentre about 10km from the town of Pitaloza Arriba in south-central Panama. According to the US Geological Survey, about 4.6 million people felt moderate to severe shaking, and the effects were likely to be widespread. The quake occurred at a depth of only 12km, which made its impact on the surface more severe.", "Videos shared online appeared to show collapsed buildings in the towns of Penonomé and Soná. In one video, a man was calling out to anyone trapped under the rubble of a collapsed building. Verified footage showed that one side of a cathedral in Penonomé had fallen, along with one of its spires, and another video showed a local hotel almost completely destroyed.", "Ricardo Brown, a 74-year-old living in Herrera province, told Reuters that several homes in his neighbourhood of Las Minas were damaged. \"We're scared. It's just the two of us old folks here. The house has cracked and we're afraid it could fall on us,\" he said. The full extent of the damage is not yet clear, and several large aftershocks were reported near the original earthquake.", "Many people were evacuated from buildings in Panama City, about 200km from the epicentre, and took to the streets or sat in nearby parks until the shaking stopped. Damage in the capital appeared limited to debris falling from roofs. President José Raúl Mulino said his whole government was mobilising, adding that the event should not be used to cause alarm or disorder.", "Tsunami warnings were initially issued for 11 neighbouring countries, but the US Tsunami Warning System later confirmed there was no threat."], "paragraphs_zh": ["地震发生在当地时间周五15:00前不久，震中位于巴拿马中南部城镇皮塔洛萨阿里巴附近约10公里处。据美国地质调查局称，约460万人感受到中度至强烈震动，影响可能很广泛。此次地震深度仅12公里，这使得其地表影响更为严重。", "网上分享的视频似乎显示佩诺诺梅和索纳等城镇有建筑物倒塌。在一段视频中，一名男子正在呼唤被困在倒塌建筑废墟下的人。经核实的视频显示，佩诺诺梅一座大教堂的一侧及其一个尖顶已经倒塌，另一段视频显示当地一家酒店几乎完全被毁。", "住在埃雷拉省的74岁老人里卡多·布朗告诉路透社，他所在的拉斯米纳斯社区有几处房屋受损。他说：“我们很害怕。这里只有我们两个老人。房子裂了，我们担心它会倒下来砸到我们。”目前损失的全部程度尚不清楚，震中附近还报告了几次强烈余震。", "在距震中约200公里的巴拿马城，许多人从建筑物中撤离，来到街上或坐在附近的公园里，直到震动停止。首都的损坏似乎仅限于屋顶掉落的碎片。总统何塞·劳尔·穆利诺表示，整个政府正在动员，并补充说，不应利用这一事件引起恐慌或混乱。", "最初对巴拿马邻国11个国家发布了海啸预警，但美国海啸预警系统后来确认没有威胁。负责管理巴拿马运河海上交通的当局表示，这条连接大西洋和太平洋的重要水道未受影响。此次地震发生前三天，巴拿马原定举行针对大地震的全国疏散演习。"], "body": "The earthquake hit just before 15:00 local time on Friday, with its epicentre about 10km from the town of Pitaloza Arriba in south-central Panama. According to the US Geological Survey, about 4.6 million people felt moderate to severe shaking, and the effects were likely to be widespread. The quake occurred at a depth of only 12km, which made its impact on the surface more severe.\n\nVideos shared online appeared to show collapsed buildings in the towns of Penonomé and Soná. In one video, a man was calling out to anyone trapped under the rubble of a collapsed building. Verified footage showed that one side of a cathedral in Penonomé had fallen, along with one of its spires, and another video showed a local hotel almost completely destroyed.\n\nRicardo Brown, a 74-year-old living in Herrera province, told Reuters that several homes in his neighbourhood of Las Minas were damaged. \"We're scared. It's just the two of us old folks here. The house has cracked and we're afraid it could fall on us,\" he said. The full extent of the damage is not yet clear, and several large aftershocks were reported near the original earthquake.\n\nMany people were evacuated from buildings in Panama City, about 200km from the epicentre, and took to the streets or sat in nearby parks until the shaking stopped. Damage in the capital appeared limited to debris falling from roofs. President José Raúl Mulino said his whole government was mobilising, adding that the event should not be used to cause alarm or disorder.\n\nTsunami warnings were initially issued for 11 neighbouring countries, but the US Tsunami Warning System later confirmed there was no threat.", "body_zh": "地震发生在当地时间周五15:00前不久，震中位于巴拿马中南部城镇皮塔洛萨阿里巴附近约10公里处。据美国地质调查局称，约460万人感受到中度至强烈震动，影响可能很广泛。此次地震深度仅12公里，这使得其地表影响更为严重。\n\n网上分享的视频似乎显示佩诺诺梅和索纳等城镇有建筑物倒塌。在一段视频中，一名男子正在呼唤被困在倒塌建筑废墟下的人。经核实的视频显示，佩诺诺梅一座大教堂的一侧及其一个尖顶已经倒塌，另一段视频显示当地一家酒店几乎完全被毁。\n\n住在埃雷拉省的74岁老人里卡多·布朗告诉路透社，他所在的拉斯米纳斯社区有几处房屋受损。他说：“我们很害怕。这里只有我们两个老人。房子裂了，我们担心它会倒下来砸到我们。”目前损失的全部程度尚不清楚，震中附近还报告了几次强烈余震。\n\n在距震中约200公里的巴拿马城，许多人从建筑物中撤离，来到街上或坐在附近的公园里，直到震动停止。首都的损坏似乎仅限于屋顶掉落的碎片。总统何塞·劳尔·穆利诺表示，整个政府正在动员，并补充说，不应利用这一事件引起恐慌或混乱。\n\n最初对巴拿马邻国11个国家发布了海啸预警，但美国海啸预警系统后来确认没有威胁。负责管理巴拿马运河海上交通的当局表示，这条连接大西洋和太平洋的重要水道未受影响。此次地震发生前三天，巴拿马原定举行针对大地震的全国疏散演习。", "text": "The earthquake hit just before 15:00 local time on Friday, with its epicentre about 10km from the town of Pitaloza Arriba in south-central Panama. According to the US Geological Survey, about 4.6 million people felt moderate to severe shaking, and the effects were likely to be widespread. The quake occurred at a depth of only 12km, which made its impact on the surface more severe. Videos shared online appeared to show collapsed buildings in the towns of Penonomé and Soná. In one video, a man was calling out to anyone trapped under the rubble of a collapsed building. Verified footage showed that one side of a cathedral in Penonomé had fallen, along with one of its spires, and another video showed a local hotel almost completely destroyed. Ricardo Brown, a 74-year-old living in Herrera province, told Reuters that several homes in his neighbourhood of Las Minas were damaged. \"We're scared. It's just the two of us old folks here. The house has cracked and we're afraid it could fall on us,\" he said. The full extent of the damage is not yet clear, and several large aftershocks were reported near the original earthquake. Many people were evacuated from buildings in Panama City, about 200km from the epicentre, and took to the streets or sat in nearby parks until the shaking stopped. Damage in the capital appeared limited to debris falling from roofs. President José Raúl Mulino said his whole government was mobilising, adding that the event should not be used to cause alarm or disorder. Tsunami warnings were initially issued for 11 neighbouring countries, but the US Tsunami Warning System later confirmed there was no threat.", "vocab": [{"word": "earthquake", "pos": "noun", "zh": "地震", "note": "常与 hit, strike, occur 等动词搭配"}, {"word": "magnitude", "pos": "noun", "zh": "震级", "note": "用于表示地震能量大小，如 magnitude 7.7"}, {"word": "epicentre", "pos": "noun", "zh": "震中", "note": "英式拼写，美式为 epicenter"}, {"word": "tremor", "pos": "noun", "zh": "轻微震动；余震", "note": "指地震引起的震动"}, {"word": "collapse", "pos": "verb", "zh": "倒塌", "note": "也可作名词，如 building collapse"}, {"word": "rubble", "pos": "noun", "zh": "瓦砾；废墟", "note": "不可数名词，常与 under 连用"}, {"word": "aftershock", "pos": "noun", "zh": "余震", "note": "主震后发生的较小地震"}, {"word": "evacuate", "pos": "verb", "zh": "疏散；撤离", "note": "常用被动语态 be evacuated"}, {"word": "debris", "pos": "noun", "zh": "碎片；残骸", "note": "不可数名词"}, {"word": "tsunami", "pos": "noun", "zh": "海啸", "note": "由地震等引发的巨浪"}, {"word": "mobilise", "pos": "verb", "zh": "动员；调动", "note": "英式拼写，美式为 mobilize"}, {"word": "waterway", "pos": "noun", "zh": "水道；航道", "note": "如巴拿马运河"}], "title_original": "Powerful magnitude 7.7 earthquake hits Panama, damaging buildings", "summary_original": "Tsunami warnings are issued for neighbouring countries as videos of destruction circulate online.", "body_original": "Powerful magnitude 7.7 earthquake hits Panama, damaging buildings\nBy\nMichael Sheils McNamee\nPublished\n9 October 2026\nA massive magnitude 7.7 earthquake has hit Panama, damaging buildings and causing widespread shaking.\nAbout 4.6 million people felt moderate to severe tremors as a result of the quake, according to the US Geological Survey, which has said that the effects of the quake were \"likely to be widespread\".\nIt struck just before 15:00 local time (18:00 GMT) on Friday, with an epicentre about 6.2 miles (10km) from the town of Pitaloza Arriba in south-central Panama.\nFootage shared online appears to show collapsed buildings in the towns of Penonomé and Soná, including one of a man calling out to anyone trapped under the rubble of a collapsed building. No casualties have so far been reported.\nVerified footage shows one side of a cathedral in Penonomé collapsed due to the shaking, as well as one of its spires.\nAnother video showed a local hotel had almost completely collapsed.\nRicardo Brown, who lives in the southern Herrera province, told news agency Reuters that the earthquake had damaged several homes in his neighbourhood of Las Minas.\n\"We're scared. It's just the two of us old folks here. The house has cracked and we're afraid it could fall on us,\" the 74-year-old said.\nThe full extent of the damage it has caused is not yet clear, though several large aftershocks were also reported near the initial earthquake, potentially complicating the situation on the surface.\nThe quake was registered as occurring at a depth of just 12km. The shallower the earthquake, the more likely it is to have more severe effects on the surface.\nMany people were evacuated from buildings in Panama City, about 200km from the epicentre, and were seen taking to the streets or sitting in nearby parks until the shaking had ceased.\nDamage in the capital appears to be limited to that caused by debris falling from roofs.\nPanama's President José Raúl Mulino said his entire government was mobilising in response to the earthquake, adding: \"What happened should not be used to cause alarm or disorder.\"\nTsunami warnings were initially issued for 11 countries neighbouring Panama, before the US Tsunami Warning System confirmed there was no threat.\nThe Panama Canal - a vital waterway linking the Atlantic and Pacific oceans - was unaffected by the earthquake, the authority that oversees marine traffic through it said.\nThe earthquake comes just three days before Panama was scheduled to hold a national evacuation drill for dealing with a major earthquake.\nIt also follows devastating earthquakes in Colombia and Venezuela earlier this year.\nRelated topics\nMexico\nEarthquakes\nChile\nPanama", "fetched_at": "2026-10-10T01:10:50.719840", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "The", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.275, "sm": 100, "em": 275, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "earthquake", "s": 0.287, "e": 0.85, "sm": 287, "em": 850, "cs": 4, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "hit", "s": 0.863, "e": 1.062, "sm": 862, "em": 1062, "cs": 15, "ce": 18, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "just", "s": 1.075, "e": 1.35, "sm": 1075, "em": 1350, "cs": 19, "ce": 23, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "before", "s": 1.363, "e": 1.688, "sm": 1362, "em": 1687, "cs": 24, "ce": 30, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "15", "s": 1.7, "e": 2.175, "sm": 1700, "em": 2175, "cs": 31, "ce": 33, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": ":", "s": 2.175, "e": 2.413, "sm": 2175, "em": 2412, "cs": 33, "ce": 34, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "00", "s": 2.413, "e": 2.888, "sm": 2412, "em": 2887, "cs": 34, "ce": 36, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "local", "s": 2.9, "e": 3.212, "sm": 2900, "em": 3212, "cs": 37, "ce": 42, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "time", "s": 3.225, "e": 3.513, "sm": 3225, "em": 3512, "cs": 43, "ce": 47, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "on", "s": 3.525, "e": 3.65, "sm": 3525, "em": 3650, "cs": 48, "ce": 50, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "Friday", "s": 3.663, "e": 4.138, "sm": 3662, "em": 4137, "cs": 51, "ce": 57, "si": 0}, {"i": 12, "w": ",", "s": 4.138, "e": 4.463, "sm": 4137, "em": 4462, "cs": 57, "ce": 58, "si": 0}, {"i": 13, "w": "with", "s": 4.463, "e": 4.625, "sm": 4462, "em": 4625, "cs": 59, "ce": 63, "si": 0}, {"i": 14, "w": "its", "s": 4.638, "e": 4.788, "sm": 4637, "em": 4787, "cs": 64, "ce": 67, "si": 0}, {"i": 15, "w": "epicentre", "s": 4.8, "e": 5.45, "sm": 4800, "em": 5450, "cs": 68, "ce": 77, "si": 0}, {"i": 16, "w": "about", "s": 5.463, "e": 5.763, "sm": 5462, "em": 5762, "cs": 78, "ce": 83, "si": 0}, {"i": 17, "w": "10", "s": 